ThinStation GitLab EE Appliance

The ISO contains one pinned upstream GitLab EE container image, retagged as:
  thinstation/gitlab-ee:appliance

Persistent state is kept on the ThinStation Docker data disk under:
  /docker/gitlab-ee/config -> /etc/gitlab
  /docker/gitlab-ee/logs   -> /var/log/gitlab
  /docker/gitlab-ee/data   -> /var/opt/gitlab

Optional persistent Compose variables may be set in:
  /docker/gitlab-ee/.env

Example:
  GITLAB_HOSTNAME=gitlab.example.org
  GITLAB_EXTERNAL_URL=https://gitlab.example.org
  GITLAB_SSH_PORT=22

Rotating to a newer GitLab appliance ISO loads the baked image and recreates
the Compose stack against the same persistent volumes. GitLab then performs
its normal version-specific upgrade/migration process.
